"The reasoning for spring follows from a point made in an earlier unit on yin-yang: the body's own yang, having spent winter stored inward, is traditionally considered still building back up to full strength even after the outdoor temperature has already warmed, making it more vulnerable to a sudden cold snap than the calendar alone would suggest. Shedding warm layers as fast as the weather warms risks exposing a yang that hasn't yet caught up. The reasoning for autumn works in the opposite direction: exposing the body to a bit of the season's early cold, rather than bundling up immediately, is traditionally considered a way of training the body's own cold tolerance gradually, before winter's harsher cold arrives in full.": "bd1e9296cc8e",
