"This piece of advice is a plain, wearable example of a habit this whole unit keeps returning to: treating the transition between seasons, not just the seasons themselves, as something worth paying deliberate attention to. A body that adjusts its clothing at the exact same pace as the thermometer, this advice suggests, is moving a little too fast in spring and a little too slow in autumn — mismatched with the body's own, slower internal adjustment to each new season.": "626059cac179",
"This unit's lessons on spring and autumn described the two seasons in terms of growth and gathering-in, but didn't address a very concrete, everyday decision shaped by that framework: what to wear as the weather itself is changing. A well-known piece of folk wellness advice addresses exactly that: \"overdress a little in spring, underdress a little in autumn,\" meaning a person should resist shedding warm clothing as quickly as spring's air warms, and resist bundling up as quickly as autumn's air cools.": "af57fe6a6ecb",
